KPI Definitions

1. Welcome Call & Intro Source Volume

Welcome Call Volume: Number of Welcome Calls executed per month, based on the Welcome Call trigger date and status.
Intro Source Volume: Number of dealers identified as eligible for an Intro Source per month, based on the Intro Source identification date.

2. Contracts & Distinct Customers per Intro Source
Median number of contracts and distinct customers associated with each Intro Source.

3. Welcome Calls Completed
Number of Welcome Calls completed per month, based on the date of the final Welcome Call outcome.

4. First-Time Customer Reach Rate
Percentage of customers successfully reached on the first call attempt.
A first-time reach is identified by a WC To Do / WC To Do with Reserve → WC OK sequence. Cancelled Welcome Calls are excluded from the calculation.

5. Welcome Call Pipeline
Number of Welcome Calls currently pending and requiring action, providing an overview of the current operational backlog.

6. Welcome Calls after Lease Start – BUTLS
Number of Welcome Calls performed after the lease start date. These cases should normally be completed before lease start and are monitored to identify and understand exceptions.

7. No E-Folder
Number of identified Welcome Calls for which no corresponding e-folder has been created within 5 days of identification.
